  "grammar_explanations": [
    {
      "slug": "present simple: adverbs of frequency (always/usually/never)",
      "title_form": "Adverbios de frecuencia",
      "title_target": "Adverbs of Frequency",
      "description_md_form": "Los **adverbios de frecuencia** nos dicen **con qué frecuencia** hacemos algo. En inglés, van **antes del verbo principal**.\n\n- **always** = siempre (100%)\n- **usually** = usualmente (80%)\n- **often** = a menudo (60%)\n- **sometimes** = a veces (40%)\n- **never** = nunca (0%)\n\n**Estructura:** `Sujeto + adverbio + verbo`\n\nEjemplos:\n- `I always drink coffee.` = Siempre tomo café.\n- `She never eats breakfast.` = Ella nunca desayuna.\n\nCon el verbo **to be**, el adverbio va **después** del verbo: `I am always happy.` = Siempre estoy feliz.",
      "description_md_target": "**Adverbs of frequency** tell us **how often** we do something. In English, they go **before the main verb**.\n\n- **always** = 100%\n- **usually** = 80%\n- **often** = 60%\n- **sometimes** = 40%\n- **never** = 0%\n\n**Structure:** `Subject + adverb + verb`\n\nExamples:\n- `I always drink coffee.`\n- `She never eats breakfast.`\n\nWith the verb **to be**, the adverb goes **after** the verb: `I am always happy.`",
      "grammar_structure": "Subject + adverb of frequency + main verb",
      "conjugation_table": {
        "name": "adverbs_of_frequency",
        "headers": [
          "Adverbio",
          "Frecuencia",
          "Ejemplo"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "always",
            "100%",
            "I always study."
          ],
          [
            "usually",
            "80%",
            "She usually walks."
          ],
          [
            "often",
            "60%",
            "We often read."
          ],
          [
            "sometimes",
            "40%",
            "He sometimes writes."
          ],
          [
            "never",
            "0%",
            "They never clean."
          ]
        ]
      },
